  "interpretation": "Coverage falls from 81.3% (permissive, |log2FC|>=0.2) to 49.5% (>=2-fold, padj<=0.01) to 24.2% (>=4-fold, padj<=0.001) on the SAME NB-GLM output. Critically, at the effect-size-gated operating point the NB-GLM returns 98/198 = 49.5%, essentially identical to the v1.0 Wilcoxon baseline (98/196 = 50%). The +31-point headline jump (50%->81.3%) is therefore largely a STRINGENCY/POWER effect, not a biological gain: the pooled-donor NB-GLM detects many small-effect (|log2FC| 0.2-1.0) signals that the per-cluster Wilcoxon test could not. The recommendation is to lead with the effect-size-gated 49.5% and present 81.3% only as the permissive-cutoff upper bound, with this grid as Supplementary evidence.",
